TYPES.md §3.1, DECISIONS 217: zz/y/w holding files of zz.y and zz, neither being zz.y.w (the
directory's own), is E2001 for the loaded zz.y, though build never loads zz; only extra.canon's
package clause is read, so zz's other, missing declaration (N, defined in zz/zz.canon, a
directory extra.canon never shares) never reaches the checker and never ICEs.
-- select --
zz.y
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- zz/zz.canon --
/// Zz.
package zz

/// N.
const N = 3
-- zz/y/y.canon --
/// Y.
package zz.y
-- zz/y/w/one.canon --
package zz.y
-- zz/y/w/extra.canon --
/// Extra: package zz, nested under zz.y.w, whose own package no file declares.
package zz

/// R.
record R {
  /// Cap.
  cap: Int(0..=N) = 0
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E2001]  zz/y/w/one.canon:1:9
  directory zz/y/w holds files of packages zz.y and zz

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
